  "discussion": {
    "headline": "cooler, drier and less humid for labor day weekend!",
    "dateLine": "11:30 a.m. Friday, September 4, 2026, Update",
    "excerpt": "As expected, multiple Mesoscale Convective Systems (MCS), or complexes of showers and heavy, gusty thunderstorms, have tracked from northwest-to-southeast through the Commonwealth along the northeastern periphery of a \"heat dome\" centered over the Southeast and Tennessee River Valley this week. On Tuesday, one such MCS was responsible for widespread wind damage in southeastern PA, the Lehigh Valley and eastern periphery of the Lower Susquehanna Valley. …",
